{
  "summary": "Rewrote Act II Chapter 14 ('The Bridge Where Friendship Died') using the Scalpel & Hose method. Final word count 1,797 (within 1,400-1,800 target window). Wrote close third past, rotating POV across four clean scene breaks: Nick on the CR125, Dr. Marsh on the bridge, Jackie inside the khakis/windbreaker, Nick alone on the circle-back. Cut all tell-after-show sentences from the source (casual cruelty, economy of teenage pride, some walls last longer, 'four bikes one pronoun'). Hosed in Hop Brook in October (amber, thin, loud only under the slate rock), the CCC bridge with the diamond-plate steel patch that rings, the two-stroke smells, the stone walls, Cavicchio's cut cornfield. Dr. Marsh glances at Nick's callused left hand (fretboard callus across the fingertip tops, wound-G scar) as a tiny unspoken crack; he looks away. Jackie's almost-smile is physical (a muscle kept ready for five years); his stepping aside is measured by his body, not his pride. Crossing prose mimics the bridge in short verb-led sentences: plate rings, planks groan, stringers shake rain-rust. Closed on a specific image — Nick alone on the warm plate, three Fender mediums clicking in his pocket, riding home past crows in Cavicchio's stubble. No ending generalization.",
  "current_status": "Act II Scalpel & Hose rewrite: Ch 14 complete at /workspace/Draft_3/scalpel_hose_rewrites/ch14_rewrite.txt. Hands off cleanly from Ch 13 (Maxanne booth pivot to 'The bridge over Hop Brook, fall of 1978'). Three other subagents handling remaining Act II chapters in parallel. Phase 2 continues."
